From f383c4a4dbf45e142a5b9ff772ab1220e2adca8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:42:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 045/128] audio: compute WE's spectrum, per channel, for
 shaders, scripts and emitters

The audio response wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485 gives wallpapers, from its capture thread (GH 0x140103630) and
frame tick (GH 0x140141520): per channel a complex FFT of max(rate/44100, 1)*1920 points (2N/3 fresh),
bins 1..639 to 64 bands (pow((i-1)/639, 0.25)*64, max per band) of sqrt(w*|X|^2) with WE's window
weight, then per frame an auto-gain per group of 8 bands, a dt-based low-pass and a rise/fall-limited
follow; the average channel, 32 and 16 bands as max of pairs.
- g_AudioSpectrum{16,32,64}{Left,Right} read their own channel (both read one mono buffer before).
- engine.registerAudioBuffers(16|32|64) returns left/right/average Float32Arrays, refreshed every
  frame; only from a module's top level, with WE's errors.
- Particle emitters with audioprocessingmode scale their rate by the loudest band of their range
  (GH 0x14025cfe0, 0x140250d80): bounds, smoothstep, exponent (a float, not an int).
- wp_context_audio_input_push takes f32 frames of any rate/channels; wp_context_audio_spectrum reads the
  bands. The u8 mono input mix still works (taken as 44.1 kHz mono). Nothing runs before any input.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md B8 (A1, A3, A4, A5, E8, S17, P20, P21)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
